Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||08-18-2001||02:24 AM||||what about using turbos from 80's early 90's 300zx's, 80's/90's supras, saab/volvo turbos, etc... also, heard dodge has a lot of good turbos- cwestco dual throttle intake manfold, 12 injectors, and 2 small turbos? saw a supra w/ 12 injectors (new one) and the second set didnt fire until engine was boosting at 10psi (and up) theres a place by me thats kind of a turbo outlet place, he rebuilds turbos and sells them, and i am trying to find a reliable turbo to build a system with- how much boost is a stock fiero computer good for? also, friend is giving me the 19lb injectors from his mustang, (20k milesm 92 5.0) these are useable in a fiero i think..||||reg||1
Z||000001||hyhy4u||08-18-2001||10:55 AM||||Turbos from the late 80's early 90's had such a bad delay on them. I used to drive a 1988 GT Turbo Sunbird Convertable..that thing had a 160 HP High OutPut 2.0 Liter L4. That thing halled...but once the turbo kicked in..by then your already a few car lengths behind..depending whta i was racing you might be able to catch up, lol.  If i was to go with a turbo i would want a newer one where the delay is a lot less.<P>- Jason.||||reg||1
Z||000002||sluppy123||08-18-2001||12:13 PM||||Turbo Lag is not really the turbos fault, it's the size of turbo and how it's plumbed into the engine.  <P>As for the twin turbo idea, are we talking about true twin turbos, one turbo for each bank of cylinders, or a sequential turbo,  two compressors hooked to one exhaust turbine. It would take alot of engineering to get a true twin turbo to fit in the engine compartment.<P>Why not just use a single T-3? or a hybrid T-3/T-4? Plenty of boost and very little turbo lag.<P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>87' GT-Galaxy silver mettalic, Turbo Charged, Modified 2.8, Eibach Sport springs, RSM side scoops, Mr Mikes leather, 17" Mille Miglia's. <BR>              <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1711832&a=12781563&p=48213929&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
